## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement defense-in-depth for cross-tenant OAuth security and a robust rollback.

## Key Concepts
- OAuth2/OIDC, Managed Identities, Conditional Access, PIM
- Private Endpoints, VNet integration, RBAC scoping
- Defender for Cloud, UEBA, alerting
- Secrets rotation and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal token validation sketch for a Node.js API
const express = require('express');
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authorize(requiredScope) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
    if (!token) return res.sendStatus(401);
    const decoded = jwt.decode(token, { complete: true });
    if (!decoded || !decoded.payload.scp?.includes(requiredScope)) return res.sendStatus(403);
    next();
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test token leakage incidents and validate rollback effectiveness?
- What telemetry and dashboards would you provision to detect anomaly token usage?

## Why This Is Asked

To assess practical cross-tenant crypto governance, KMS design, and audit controls in Azure for enterprise buyers like Oracle, MongoDB, Hugging Face.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant KEKs in Azure Key Vault
- Envelope encryption with DEKs
- RBAC and data masking
- Auditing and rollback planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: fetch tenant DEK from Key Vault and wrap data
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { KeyClient, CryptographyClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-keys');

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const keyClient = new KeyClient(`https://${vaultName}.vault.azure.net`, credential);
const key = await keyClient.getKey(tenantDekName);
const cryptoClient = new CryptographyClient(key.id, credential);
const wrapped = await cryptoClient.wrapKey('RSA-OAEP', dek);
```

